# `best = list[k] < best ? list[k] : best` loads the element once: the second read is the value of the first. What is left of the second read is the patchpoint that keeps the array alive. It is no code,
# so it does not hold the branch: it goes in front of the select, and the loop is the one of `const value = list[k]; best = value < best ? value : best`.
# CHECK-LABEL: steps by 8
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# REPEAT: turn = 1..8
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[value%(turn)]] = Load(b@{{*}}Reads:TypedArrayElements
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isSmaller%(turn)]] = LessThan(b@[[value%(turn)]], b@[[best%(turn)]], {{*}}:Less)
# CHECK-NEXT: Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:ColdAny, runsWithoutFrame, resultConstraints = WarmAny, WritesLocalState|Reads:Top, {{*}}:GetTypedArrayElement)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@{{*}} = Select(b@[[isSmaller%(turn)]], b@[[value%(turn)]], b@[[best%(turn)]]
# END REPEAT
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK: Branch(b@{{*}}, Terminal, {{*}}:Less)
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 18, patchpoints: 16, {{*}} steps by 8
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 19, patchpoints: 16, {{*}} steps by 8
